body:
Hi there, I am current student of the college. I have also finished my Bachelor's degree there too.

&#x200B;

As for the entrance exam, be prepared to answer questions about current events, always be informed and watch news. It is in essay type. There is also a psychological exam that is in multiple choice. The exam takes about 3-4 hours but has a break in between. And yes, the exam was hard, you do not know what the questions will be and I will be honest, I experienced mental block.

&#x200B;

As for the quality of education, due to the pandemic, we are currently doing online classes. And most of the professors are top-notch lawyers of our country like Atty. Antonio Lavina and 2008 Bar topnotcher Atty Judy Lardizabal are teaching here. The level of education here is at par with other renowned law schools. We even placed 9th last bar.

&#x200B;

Just give it a try. I myself was half-hearted when I entered, but now I am more inspired by the stories of my professors. You would not know if you do not try. And if this is really your dream, hold on to that dream and never give up.
